  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable and Gender Sensitive Integration of IDPs in Pemba through the Implementation of Urban Durable Solutions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a joint project between IOM and UN-HABITAT in Mozambique to address the needs of, and contribute to pathways to Durable Solutions for Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) within the greater Pemba area in Cabo Delgado Province. The project takes a Gender Sensitive approach to the Integration of IDPs in an urban setting, through the following components: Engaging communities in participatory and gender-inclusive planning and management at municipal and neighborhood scale; Awareness rising on specific social services provision; Improving living conditions for vulnerable women and girls within host communities and IDPs at the neighbourhood scale through assisted self-construction of prioritized community infrastructure, including on-the-job training and employment / entrepreneurship opportunities; Increasing institutional capacities of local authorities; Increasing livelihood opportunities for communities; Monitoring and evaluation to extract lessons learned and formulate guidelines for scaling-up of future Durable Solutions programming; Increasing access to MHPSS services in the Mahate neighbourhood for host and displaced communities; and Improving peaceful co-existence between host and displaced communities through socio-relational activities.</narrative>
  </description>
